// Local.xcconfig.example -- the template for Local.xcconfig.
//
// Copy it to Local.xcconfig and edit the copy. Local.xcconfig is gitignored;
// this file is not, so nothing you put HERE stays private.
//
//     cp Local.xcconfig.example Local.xcconfig
//
// A committed DEVELOPMENT_TEAM builds on one Mac and fails everywhere else
// with a provisioning error that does not explain itself, which is why the
// signing identity lives outside the project.
//
// This file is included LAST by Dev.xcconfig and Release.xcconfig, so anything
// set here overrides the committed defaults.

// ---- Required -------------------------------------------------------------
// Your Apple Developer Team ID. Xcode > Settings > Accounts, or the membership
// page at developer.apple.com. A free personal Apple ID has one too.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOUR_TEAM_ID

// ---- Optional: build under your own identifiers ---------------------------
// Uncomment and change the prefix if `com.joshuajones.Hearth` is not yours to
// sign -- which it is not, unless you are Joshua. A bundle identifier already
// registered to another team cannot be claimed by yours, and the failure reads
// as a provisioning problem rather than a naming one.
//
// Change the prefix ONLY. The three bundle identifiers derive from it:
//
//     <prefix>            the iOS app
//     <prefix>.Widgets    the widget extension
//     <prefix>Vision      the visionOS app
//
// HEARTH_ID_PREFIX = com.yourname.Hearth
// HEARTH_APP_GROUP = group.com.yourname.Hearth
//
// The app group is a separate line because it is a separate capability, and on
// a FREE personal team it is not available at all. That is fine today -- the
// project does not sign entitlements yet -- but it is the reason the widgets
// will not work on a free account when they land.
